## Git and completion

- Create a branch before changes using `<work-type>/<short-description>`, such
  as `feature/article-pages`, `fix/preview-permissions`, or `docs/setup`.
  Continue an existing task branch when appropriate; do not work directly on main.
- Preserve unrelated user work. Keep changes focused and never discard local
  edits or rewrite shared Git history without explicit authorization.
- Review the final diff for accidental changes, secrets, missing migrations,
  and missing tests. Update the README or relevant docs for changed behaviour.
- Report what changed, which checks ran and their outcomes, and any remaining
  limitations or migration/deployment steps. Never imply that unrun checks passed.
